+# 1Password + OpenRouter Setup
+
+**Scope:** local developer machine for `IDAHO-VAULT`  
+**Status:** active template  
+**Updated:** 2026-04-21
+
+## Goal
+
+This repo standardizes on:
+
+- `op` for secret and credential retrieval
+- OpenRouter for OpenAI-compatible model routing
+- `op run` as the default way to inject secrets into local agent sessions
+
+The repo does **not** store plaintext API keys.
+
+## Local assumptions
+
+- Windows user account without administrator privileges
+- Git for Windows already installed
+- 1Password desktop app installed and signed in
+- `codex` available on the machine
+
+## 1. Install or verify `op`
+
+Preferred on this machine:
+
+```powershell
+scoop install 1password-cli
+op --version
+```
+
+If `op` is already on `PATH`, do not reinstall it.
+
+Useful check:
+
+```powershell
+where.exe op
+op whoami
+```
+
+## 2. Authenticate 1Password CLI
+
+For local interactive use, prefer desktop-app auth:
+
+```powershell
+op signin
+op vault list
+```
+
+For automation or shared runners, use a service account token:
+
+```powershell
+$env:OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN="..."
+op whoami
+```
+
+Relevant 1Password env vars:
+
+- `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN`
+- `OP_ACCOUNT`
+- `OP_CONFIG_DIR`
+
+## 3. Create the required 1Password items
+
+Create these items in the `IDAHO-VAULT` vault, or adjust the secret references if the vault name differs.
+
+Required now:
+
+- `OpenRouter API Key`
+  - field: `credential`
+
+Recommended next:
+
+- `GitHub Personal Access Token`
+  - field: `credential`
+- `Linear API Key`
+  - field: `credential`
+
+You can confirm the OpenRouter item resolves with:
+
+```powershell
+op read "op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential"
+```
+
+## 4. Use the repo env template
+
+This repo ships a template file at `.op/openrouter.env.template`.
+
+Create a working copy that stays local:
+
+```powershell
+Copy-Item .op\openrouter.env.template .op\openrouter.env
+```
+
+The file contains 1Password secret references, not plaintext secrets.
+
+## 5. Launch Codex through 1Password
+
+From the repo root:
+
+```powershell
+op run --env-file=".op\openrouter.env" -- codex --profile openrouter
+```
+
+Or use the helper script:
+
+```cmd
+!\launch-codex-openrouter.cmd
+```
+
+This will:
+
+- resolve the OpenRouter API key from 1Password
+- set the OpenAI-compatible endpoint to OpenRouter
+- launch Codex with the repo-scoped `openrouter` profile
+
+## 6. Repo config behavior
+
+The project-scoped Codex config lives at `.codex/config.toml`.
+
+The `openrouter` profile uses:
+
+- provider: `openai`
+- base URL: `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`
+- auth mode: API key
+
+The active model remains configurable. Start with:
+
+- `openrouter/auto` for model routing
+
+If you later want a pinned model, set `OPENAI_MODEL` in `.op/openrouter.env`.
+
+## 7. Operational pattern
+
+Use this pattern for any local tool that accepts env vars:
+
+```powershell
+op run --env-file=".op\openrouter.env" -- <command>
+```
+
+Examples:
+
+```powershell
+op run --env-file=".op\openrouter.env" -- codex --profile openrouter
+op run --env-file=".op\openrouter.env" -- cmd /c echo %OPENAI_BASE_URL%
+```
+
+## 8. Notes on 1Password Environments
+
+If the team later standardizes on 1Password Environments instead of item references, `op run --environment <ENV_ID> -- ...` is a valid upgrade path.
+
+This repo is starting with secret references because they work with the stable `op` flow and require less organizational setup.
+
+## 9. Troubleshooting
+
+`op: command not found`
+
+- Verify Scoop install and user `PATH`
+- Restart the shell after installation
+
+`op whoami` fails
+
+- Sign in with the desktop app using `op signin`
+- Or provide `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN`
+
+`codex` starts but cannot authenticate
+
+- Confirm `OPENAI_API_KEY` resolves from `.op/openrouter.env`
+- Confirm the launch command uses `op run`
+- Confirm the active profile is `openrouter`
+
+`OpenRouter returns auth or quota errors`
+
+- Verify the API key item value in 1Password
+- Verify OpenRouter account credits and model access
+
+## References
+
+- 1Password `op run`: https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/reference/commands/run
+- 1Password secret references: https://developer.1password.com/docs/cli/secret-reference-syntax
+- OpenRouter authentication: https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/authentication
+- OpenRouter model routing: https://openrouter.ai/docs/model-routing
