+---
+name: 1Password Secrets Reference
+description: Current project secrets inventory for 1Password-managed local and automation workflows
+type: reference
+---
+
+# Secrets Inventory
+
+**Vault:** `IDAHO-VAULT`  
+**Primary loader:** `op run --env-file`  
+**Updated:** 2026-04-21
+
+## Required now
+
+| Secret Name | Field | Used By | Status | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `OpenRouter API Key` | `credential` | Codex OpenRouter profile | Required | Stored in 1Password; exposed at runtime as `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` |
+
+## Recommended next
+
+| Secret Name | Field | Used By | Status | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `GitHub Personal Access Token` | `credential` | GitHub API / automation | Recommended | Fetch via `op run` rather than storing in local shells |
+| `Linear API Key` | `credential` | Linear sync and automation | Recommended | Keep off disk; retrieve only in the process that needs it |
+| `OP Service Account Token` | `credential` | CI or headless access | Optional | Prefer only for automation, not day-to-day local use |
+
+## Secret reference examples
+
+OpenRouter key:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential
+```
+
+GitHub token:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/GitHub Personal Access Token/credential
+```
+
+Linear key:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/Linear API Key/credential
+```
+
+## Runtime mapping
+
+The repo template `.op/openrouter.env.template` maps:
+
+- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` -> OpenRouter key from 1Password
+- `OPENAI_API_KEY` -> same OpenRouter key for OpenAI-compatible clients
+- `OPENAI_BASE_URL` -> `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`
+- `OPENAI_MODEL` -> `openrouter/auto`
+
+## Rotation guidance
+
+| Secret | Rotation |
+|---|---|
+| OpenRouter API Key | Rotate on exposure, role change, or billing/security concern |
+| GitHub PAT | 90 days |
+| Linear API Key | 180 days |
+| Service account token | 90 days |
+
+## Local verification
+
+Verify a secret resolves:
+
+```powershell
+op read "op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential"
+```
+
+Verify the env file injects values:
+
+```powershell
+op run --env-file=".op\openrouter.env" -- cmd /c echo %OPENAI_BASE_URL%
+```
+
+## Rules
+
+- Do not commit plaintext secrets.
+- Prefer `op run` over long-lived exported env vars.
+- Keep reusable secret references in templates, not actual secret values.
+- Prefer one item per credential so rotation is obvious.
