*** Update File: C:\Users\loganf\Documents\IDAHO-VAULT\.op\SETUP.md
@@
-## 3. Create the required 1Password items
-
-Create these items in the `IDAHO-VAULT` vault, or adjust the secret references if the vault name differs.
-
-Required now:
-
-- `OpenRouter API Key`
-  - field: `credential`
-
-Recommended next:
-
-- `GitHub Personal Access Token`
-  - field: `credential`
-- `Linear API Key`
-  - field: `credential`
-
-You can confirm the OpenRouter item resolves with:
-
-```powershell
-op read "op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential"
-```
+## 3. Normalize by reference, not by display name
+
+Do not depend on friendly item titles or field labels if your vault is messy.
+
+Use one of these approaches:
+
+- best: create a clean dedicated item for each active credential
+- acceptable: keep the existing item, but reference it by stable item ID and field label or field ID
+
+For this repo, the canonical target is one OpenRouter secret that resolves into:
+
+- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`
+- `OPENAI_API_KEY`
+
+If you want to inspect an existing item and its fields:
+
+```powershell
+op item get "<item name or item id>" --format json
+```
+
+If you want stable identifiers, list items and copy the relevant IDs:
+
+```powershell
+op item list --vault "IDAHO-VAULT" --format json
+```
+
+Then prefer secret references like:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/<ITEM_ID>/<FIELD_ID_OR_LABEL>
+```
+
+Example:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/abc123xyz789/credential
+```
+
+If the field is oddly named, that is fine. The repo only cares that the reference resolves.
@@
-## 4. Use the repo env template
+## 4. Use the repo env template
@@
-The file contains 1Password secret references, not plaintext secrets.
+The file contains 1Password secret references, not plaintext secrets.
+
+If your existing item names are inconsistent, edit `.op/openrouter.env` to use item IDs instead of titles.
@@
-## 9. Troubleshooting
+## 9. Minimal cleanup strategy
+
+Do not try to clean the entire vault first. Normalize only the credentials that are actually on the hot path.
+
+Recommended order:
+
+1. OpenRouter API key
+2. GitHub PAT
+3. Linear API key
+
+For each one:
+
+1. Identify the current item and field that actually work.
+2. Record the stable secret reference in your local env file.
+3. Later, rename or replace the item when convenient.
+
+## 10. Troubleshooting
*** Update File: C:\Users\loganf\Documents\IDAHO-VAULT\.op\secrets.template.md
@@
 ## Secret reference examples
 
 OpenRouter key:
 
 ```text
 op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential
 ```
+
+Stable-ID variant:
+
+```text
+op://IDAHO-VAULT/<OPENROUTER_ITEM_ID>/<OPENROUTER_FIELD_ID_OR_LABEL>
+```
@@
 Linear key:
 
 ```text
 op://IDAHO-VAULT/Linear API Key/credential
 ```
+
+## Preferred practice
+
+- Use item names only if the vault is already clean.
+- Use item IDs when titles are inconsistent.
+- Use field IDs or exact field labels when fields are oddly named.
+- Keep the normalization in `.op/openrouter.env`, not in code.
@@
 The repo template `.op/openrouter.env.template` maps:
@@
 - `OPENAI_MODEL` -> `openrouter/auto`
+
+You are expected to replace the placeholder OpenRouter reference in your local `.op/openrouter.env` with the real working secret reference for your vault.
*** Update File: C:\Users\loganf\Documents\IDAHO-VAULT\.op\openrouter.env.template
@@
-OPENROUTER_API_KEY=op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential
-OPENAI_API_KEY=op://IDAHO-VAULT/OpenRouter API Key/credential
+# Replace <OPENROUTER_SECRET_REF> with the exact working 1Password secret reference.
+# Prefer item IDs over titles if your vault naming is inconsistent.
+OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<OPENROUTER_SECRET_REF>
+OPENAI_API_KEY=<OPENROUTER_SECRET_REF>
 OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
 OPENAI_MODEL=openrouter/auto
*** End Patch
