+# LAF-USB - Disambiguation
+
+`LAF-USB` has existing vault meaning before the Universal Sync Bus connector
+work. In the historical migration context, `LAF-USB` names both a Five Cores
+migration current and a live GitHub team surface under the LAF-PUBLIC topology.
+
+Do not collapse the team/migration label into the transport protocol. When the
+intended meaning is the external-object connector, write [[Universal Sync Bus]]
+or [[LAF-USB-PROTOCOL-FRAMEWORK]]. When the intended meaning is the team or
+migration current, link this note or
+[[!-LAF-USB-FIVE-CORES-MIGRATION-2026-04-15]].
+
+## DOCUMENT METADATA
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-08
+- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-08
+- **Status:** Active
+- **Authority:** LOGAN
+- **Change Note:** Added Obsidian-native disambiguation for LAF-USB.
*** Add File: C:\Users\loganf\Documents\IDAHO-VAULT-pushable\Universal Sync Bus.md
+---
+title: "Universal Sync Bus"
+updated: 2026-05-08
+status: staged
+authority: "LOGAN"
+aliases:
+  - USB (Universal Sync Bus)
+related:
+  - USB
+  - LAF-USB
+  - LAF-USB-PROTOCOL-FRAMEWORK
+  - VAULT-MEDIA-STORAGE
+  - DISTRIBUTED-HASH-LEDGER
+  - BACKUP-INFRASTRUCTURE-OPERATION-SYNTHESIS
+---
+
+# Universal Sync Bus
+
+Universal Sync Bus is the vault transport/reference concept for objects that
+need durable tracking across Git, GitHub, local filesystems, cloud remotes,
+and cold storage without treating a local drive letter or one provider URL as
+the object's identity.
+
+Markdown carries the doctrine, aliases, wikilinks, source context, and human
+record. JSON carries the object manifest. Python validates the manifest and
+tooling behavior. Jupyter may bridge Markdown and Python for literate,
+runnable inspection, but the notebook still needs a Markdown node so Obsidian
+can see the concept.
+
+See [[LAF-USB-PROTOCOL-FRAMEWORK]] for the staged protocol details.
+
+## DOCUMENT METADATA
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-08
+- **Last Updated:** 2026-05-08
+- **Status:** Staged
+- **Authority:** LOGAN
+- **Change Note:** Added canonical concept note for the Universal Sync Bus.
*** End Patch
